{
  "version": 1,
  "generation": 2,
  "notes": "Synthetic Gen2 mechanic vectors for Lua/JS BattleSim2 parity. No ROM data: no species, move, ability or item names — only integer ids and type indices. All arithmetic is integer. DAMAGE (pokecrystal BattleCommand_DamageCalc): no 255-stat clamp inside compute(), which takes the byte pair TruncateHL_BC hands it (see TRUNCATE). levelTerm = floor(2L/5)+2 (crit does NOT double L). base = floor(floor(levelTerm*power*attack/defense)/50). Then optional item boost, crit x2, then min(d,997)+2. STAB floor(d*15/10). Type effectiveness is a list of percents applied one at a time as floor(d*pct/100) with a non-immune floor of 1. Variation last: when modified>=2, damage=max(1,min(999,floor(d*roll/100))) for roll in 85..100. Physical reads attack/atk; special (physical:false) reads spa (legacy spc) vs spd (legacy spc). CRIT: ladder 1-in-{15,8,4,3,2,2,2} by critical level 0..6; isCrit when roll==0 for roll in 0..chance-1. Level += focusEnergy(+1), highCritMove(+2), scopeLens(+1), speciesItemBonus(+2), capped at 6. ACCURACY: percent domain; accuracy 0 or alwaysHits never misses; else value=stage-scaled accuracy clamped 1..100, hit = roll < value for roll in 0..99 (no Gen1 1/256 miss). STATUS: freeze thaws when roll%5==0 (1/5); burn/poison residual max(1,floor(maxHp/8)); burn halves physical attack; toxic max(1,floor(maxHp*counter/16)); paralysis stops when roll%4==0 (1/4); sleep wakes and can move when the counter hits 0. BADGES (Crystal, as gen1recomp src/battle/gen2/Battle.lua ports it): badgeStats is Effects.badgeBoost(stat, key, badges, spa) -> value, badges a set of Gold ids. ZEPHYR->atk, MINERAL->def, PLAIN->spe, GLACIER->spa, each boostStat = min(999, v + floor(v/8)); Kanto ids boost no stat; spd only when GLACIER is held and glacierBoostsSpDef(boostStat(spa)): true at >= 999, else a = (floor(v/256) - 3 - (v%256 < 231 ? 1 : 0)) mod 256 and boosted when a is odd. badgeTypes is Effects.badgeTypeBoost(typeId, badges) -> boosted: the first of the 16 DoBadgeTypeBoosts rows naming typeId (registry id, PSYCHIC_TYPE for Psychic) answers whether its badge is held. Damage's badgeTypeBoost adds max(1, floor(d/8)) right after the 997+2 tail and before STAB. STAGES (pokecrystal CalcBattleStats): stages is Effects.applyStage(stat, stage) -> value = floor(stat*pct/100) for the stage percent (25,28,33,40,50,66,100,150,200,250,300,350,400), then 0 -> 1 and anything past 999 -> 999. BATTLESTATS (CalcPlayerStats): battleStats is Effects.battleStat({stats, stages, status}, key, badges) -> value: applyStage, then the badge boost (spd's Glacier tail reads boostStat of the STAGED spa), then burn halves atk / paralysis quarters spe, each at least 1. TRUNCATE (TruncateHL_BC): truncate is Damage.truncateStats(attack, defense, link) -> attack, defense: while either is over 255, defense = floor(defense/4) and attack = floor(attack/4), each 0 -> 1; link stops after one pass; both come out mod 256 (the wrap bug). STATUS confusion: a self-hit is Damage.compute at power 40 with no crit, STAB or matchup and roll 100 (no variation) on the attack/defense given, plus itemBoostPercent when given.",
